    "result_text": "All 22 tests pass with a green build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` on `POST /api/owners`, returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`: the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName **and** lastName, compared case-insensitively.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `customerCode` / `householdId` computed fields):\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount.java` counts persisted owners matching the new owner's first+last name (case-insensitively) via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`. It runs before `SaveOwner` within the same write transaction, so it naturally excludes the not-yet-saved new owner and reflects the state immediately before the insert.\n\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 inserted `assignNamesakeCount` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into `owners.POST.yml` between `assignHouseholdId` and `save`.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column-mapped `Integer namesakeCount` field with getter/setter to `Owner`.\n\n4. **DTO / API** \u2014 added `namesakeCount` (readonly `int32`) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it Owner\u2192Dto automatically. Added `@Mapping(target = \"namesakeCount\", ignore = true)` to `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` since it's server-assigned, not client input.\n\n5. **Schema** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql); hsqldb is the one exercised by the test profile.\n\nThe new `Cp13Tests` passes, and all 22 tests across the suite remain green.",
